# Criterion 6: the copy-paste template ships no vacuous assertions

The template is the file forks copy when they wire up Firebase
Performance; it carried 14 `expect(true, isTrue)` calls that propagated
the pattern outward.

$ grep -c 'expect(true, isTrue)' test/shared/performance/firebase_performance_service_test.dart.template
0
(exit 1)

What replaced them (operations now assert they ran; swallow-the-exception cases assert the call was still attempted):

$ grep -n 'expect(ran, isTrue)\|returnsNormally);\|verify(() => mockTrace' test/shared/performance/firebase_performance_service_test.dart.template | cat
110:        expect(ran, isTrue);
157:        expect(ran, isTrue);
267:        expect(ran, isTrue);
294:        expect(ran, isTrue);
308:        expect(ran, isTrue);
323:        expect(ran, isTrue);
346:        expect(ran, isTrue);
391:        verify(() => mockTrace.start()).called(1);
399:        verify(() => mockTrace.start()).called(1);
407:        verify(() => mockTrace.start()).called(1);
413:        expect(performanceTrace.startSync, returnsNormally);
414:        verify(() => mockTrace.start()).called(1);
422:        verify(() => mockTrace.stop()).called(1);
429:        verify(() => mockTrace.stop()).called(1);
437:        verify(() => mockTrace.stop()).called(1);
443:        expect(performanceTrace.stopSync, returnsNormally);
444:        verify(() => mockTrace.stop()).called(1);
452:        verify(() => mockTrace.incrementMetric('success', 1)).called(1);
464:        verify(() => mockTrace.incrementMetric('success', 1)).called(1);
472:        verify(() => mockTrace.incrementMetric('success', 1)).called(1);
484:        verify(() => mockTrace.incrementMetric('success', 1)).called(1);
492:        verify(() => mockTrace.putAttribute('key', 'value')).called(1);
504:        verify(() => mockTrace.putAttribute('key', 'value')).called(1);
512:        verify(() => mockTrace.putAttribute('key1', 'value1')).called(1);
513:        verify(() => mockTrace.putAttribute('key2', 'value2')).called(1);
(exit 0)

